---
import BaseLayout from '@/components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '@/lib/tools';

const roadmapCount = TOOLS.filter((tool) => !tool.live).length;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About SoloYolo"
  description="Who builds SoloYolo, how every calculator works, and why the tools are free, private and exact."
  path="/about/"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />

    <article class="max-w-3xl pt-8 pb-16 sm:pt-12">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-[clamp(2.1rem,1.4rem+3.4vw,3.4rem)] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em]">
        Business tools that respect your work
      </h1>

      <div class="prose-ledger mt-10">
        <p>
          SoloYolo is a suite of free business calculators and document generators for freelancers,
          consultants, creators, contractors and small service businesses in the United States,
          United Kingdom, Canada, Australia, Germany, Switzerland, India and the United Arab
          Emirates.
        </p>
        <p>
          The first tool, the <a href="/calculators/hourly-rate-calculator/">hourly rate
          calculator</a>, answers a question almost every independent professional gets wrong:
          what hourly rate actually covers your target income, your business costs, and all the
          hours you cannot invoice. {roadmapCount} more tools (rates, margins, taxes and
          professional documents) are on the roadmap and ship only after their maths is covered
          by automated tests.
        </p>

        <h2>How the tools work</h2>
        <p>
          Every calculation runs entirely in your browser. There is no backend, no account and no
          upload: your income targets, client names and invoice details never leave your device.
          Financial results are computed with exact decimal arithmetic rather than binary floating
          point, and every formula is covered by unit tests for normal values, zero, negatives,
          rounding and extreme inputs.
        </p>
        <p>
          The numbers printed in worked examples are computed by the same engine the tool uses, so
          what you read on a page can never drift from what the tool produces.
        </p>

        <h2>How SoloYolo is funded</h2>
        <p>
          The tools are free. The site is funded by advertising: when you accept ads in the cookie
          banner, Google AdSense may show ads on these pages. Ads are clearly labelled, never
          disguised as content or tools, and never required to use a calculator: with "essential
          only" cookies, no ad scripts load at all.
        </p>

        <h2>Principles</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Private by default.</strong> No account, no tracking of your inputs, no selling of data.</li>
          <li><strong>Exact, not approximate.</strong> Decimal math, tested formulas, honest rounding.</li>
          <li><strong>No dark patterns.</strong> No paywalled results, no fake urgency, no forced email capture.</li>
          <li><strong>Advice-free.</strong> Calculators are informational tools, not tax, accounting or legal advice.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Get in touch</h2>
        <p>
          Found a bug, a wrong number or a missing tool? Write to
          <a href="mailto:hello@soloyolo.example">hello@soloyolo.example</a>, or see the
          <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> for what to include.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
